            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 331,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I messed this up before with the bmcweb one.  You really want this version as part of the filename, so if say, you wanted to change this to parse yaml instead of json, you could prior to actually parsing.\n\nAlso, while you're parsing you can know what version happens."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 331,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Hmm, is that something in a best practices guide? I haven't seen it before. I get the point but it feels like a bit much here. This is a very simple json file and I don't see why we'd ever go away from json. Also, adding the version to the file adds some complexity when it comes to cleaning up older versions of the file. My preference is to just leave it as it is here but I'll give some other people time to weigh in."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 331,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "The idea of putting the version in the file name has some merit to it but I'd prefer to see a broader discussion in a best practices review. For now, lets just go with the version within the json as it's simple and allows for removing the older versions files easier."
                }
            ],
